speechtext:
1. (a) Contributions until 31 December, 1968, total $974,628.26, composed of the following: (i) To Biafra through Santa Isabel November, 1968, $312,218.80; (ii) To Nigeria for Refugees: August, 1968, $63,720.00; November, 1968, $538,699.46; Total, $602,419.46. (iii) By cash to International Committee of the Red Cross, $60,000. (b) Contributions during 1969 total $1,719,103, composed of the following, (i) To Biafra through Santa Isabel, $752,201.55; (ii) To Nigeria for Refugees, $926,901.45; (iii) By cash to I.C.R.C. $40,000.
2. Contributions to December 31, 1968: (i) To Biafra direct through Santa Isabel, 1262 metric tons dried fish; (ii) to Nigeria for Refugees, 4 metric tons medicaments and 1267 metric tons dried fish; (iii) $60,000 cash contribution to International Committee of the Red Cross for use in the Nigeria/Biafra areas for refugees. (No breakdown of actual use available.) 1969 Contributions: (i) To Biafra direct through Santa Isabel, 927 metric tons dried fish and 40 metric tons potato granules;
(ii)	To Nigeria for Refugees, 1183 metric tons dried fish and 600 metric tons potato granules;
(iii)	$40,000 cash contribution to International Committee of the Red Cross for use in the Nigeria/Biafra areas for refugees. (No breakdown of actual use available).
